// Negative fixture (guard reject): sound definite assignment through
// switch — a switch without an else keeps the no-match path unassigned, so
// the trailing read must be rejected before the program runs, even for a
// variable initialized before the switch (parity with the compilers).
// Expected pre-run diagnostic: GuardError: UnassignedVariableCallException ...

void main() {
    int y = 1;
    switch (9) {
        case 1 { y = 100; }
    }
    printline(y);
}
